From afd15a39e820dc69d3921a64f735d97f202740cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan Hawkley <dan@triplettrustprotocol.net>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:29:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] B2: density, positivity, minimal period and the W-trick,
 kernel-checked

Adds the Challenge/Solution pair MultiShiftB2 with nine statements:
relative density (B1's absolute density times m), local positivity, a
minimal-period theorem extending gdt_minimal_period to every nonempty
shift set, two counterexamples showing its extra hypotheses (H nonempty,
accepted set nonempty) are both necessary, the W-trick count of
Definition 4.5, the equivalence of section 2 admissibility with positive
local factors, and the W-trick for H45: a residue exists for every W, and
at W = 2*3*...*23 it is unique, b = 74549147.

The minimal-period search script and its results are recorded in
specs/checks/minimal_period_search.py and specs/results/B2_multishift.yaml.

